    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into May 23rd with a calculated offensive strategy anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (77.58) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Kyle Tucker** remains our most potent asset today; despite facing a lefty in Robert Gasser, the soft matchup against a 5.63 xERA pitcher provides enough upside to overcome platoon stagnation. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% dynamic platoon boost against a middling arm in Holmes, securing his spot as a primary driver of our daily efficiency. The high-upside play of the day is **Sam Antonacci** (67.67), whose leadoff spot and favorable wind conditions contribute to an elite 0.397 xwOBA profile, making him a critical engine for Runs and the high-priority Stolen Base category we are targeting to remain competitive in 5x5 Roto.\n\nWe have opted to bench **Nolan Schanuel** (41.64), who represents the narrowest cut of the day. While **Nolan Schanuel** maintains a stable floor, the optimizer prioritized the aggressive matchups of **Andy Pages** and **Dominic Smith**, both of whom benefit from superior SP xERA environments. Our lineup construction faced a severe hurdle with the confirmed rainout of **Gunnar Henderson**, and we continue to navigate around the extended absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**. Furthermore, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73) remains in the lineup as a UTIL option, we are wary of his matchup against Skenes; that 2.96 xERA is the most dangerous obstacle on our board, and his score reflects a significant downward adjustment for elite opposing pitching that could threaten our AVG stability.",
